sourceReview.sourceLayoutEvidence:
The source has two equally prominent location panels. Each heading and statistic scaffold starts at the left of its panel; its dot plot sits to the right beside the upper responses. Median and mean responses extend below the plot. Both plots retain all six ticks, identical horizontal spacing, black observation markers and the complete axis title. The executable arrangement preserves these relationships and keeps a and b below both panels. All statistic response children have explicit empty structural labels. The original blue supplied responses are stored separately from student prompts; practice short answers inherit ordinary ink. Filled circles are data markers, and no diagram area shading is introduced. Handwriting estimates are editable: 10 mm for a range calculation or modes; 20 mm for counting central positions and averaging the middle pair; 26 mm for summing observations and dividing by 14; 12 mm for each full-width comparison. These are solution-informed estimates, not measured source dimensions.
